{"reference":"Genesis 3","book":"Genesis","chapter":3,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Adam and Eve in later interpretation","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"A later epistolary reading invokes Adam's prior formation and Eve's deception, but interpreters dispute how that reading grounds a local or universal rule. That dispute cautions against treating a reception-history argument as though Genesis 3 itself stated the later conclusion in those terms.","verse_refs":["Genesis 3:1-24"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_genesis_003_08bca9652b7f96196e219fe9"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}
